# muse client support (Meta Muse Code CLI) — umbrella

## Goal

Comprehensive c2c support for `muse` (Meta Muse Code CLI, probed at
v1.4.2) with cross-client parity: a Muse → Claude/Codex send Just Works,
same envelope, same delivery honesty. Tiers ship in order; each tier is
independently useful.

## Background (measured 2026-10-02, read-only recon)

- Binary: `muse` bash launcher + `muse-bin` payload. Key subcommands:
  `session-message`, `mcp`, `plugins`, `skills`, `exec`, `serve`, `resume`.
- MCP stdio is real and documented: `settings.json` key `mcpServers`
  (camelCase), stdio shape with `mode:"optional"`. No channel/push
  extension → MCP is poll-tools. Gotchas: dual `mcpServers`+`mcp_servers`
  keys drop the whole member; no `${VAR}` expansion; next-launch-only.
- Hooks: documented native-plugin contract (manifest
  `.muse-plugin/plugin.json`, events SessionStart/PreToolUse/PostToolUse/
  SessionEnd/…, `plugins validate|install|approve|hook test --fixture`).
  `settings.json` `hooks.handlers` recognized, handler schema unverified.
- Wake primitive exists but gated: `muse session-message send --target`
  unlocks ONLY via `MUSE_EXPERIMENTAL_EXTERNAL_AGENT_INGRESS=1`
  (env-only; no persistent switch found). Live delivery untested.
- Managed start feasible: `muse exec` headless works (keep session
  logging ON); interactive needs a TTY → tmux/herdr pty + kickoff;
  untrusted cwd needs `--trust-workspace`.
- **Nothing is impossible.** Two load-bearing unknowns gate Tier-1/2
  scope and are owned by the B352 spike (operator-run live probes).

Full evidence: `.collab/research/2026-10-02T17-25-36Z-muse-client-support-scout.md`
(scout synthesis: per-surface file:line checklists, IGC matrices D1–D4,
unknowns register U1–U10). Five scout reports back it; their /tmp
originals are ephemeral — the research doc is the durable reference.

